repository-code: "https://github.com/LeoLam233/ising-bulk-natural-boundary"
abstract: "Four mathematical developments on natural boundaries of the complete square-lattice Ising bulk susceptibility: separate isotropic low- and high-temperature results, fixed-positive-ratio anisotropic results covering both phases, and a two-independent-complex-coupling parent theorem with physical-slice descendants. The repository provides complete reviewed Reader manuscripts, unchanged original mathematical sources, Lean formalizations, explicit physical-input interfaces, and reproducibility and audit records. Manuscript-only conclusions are distinguished from actual formal theorem endpoints. The repository's software is licensed under MIT; author-created manuscripts and documentation are under CC BY 4.0."
